# Baseline: everything ships LF. `npm publish` from Windows shipped CRLF in
# 1.4.2, which broke the `#!/usr/bin/env node` shebang on macOS/Linux — the
# package was dead on arrival there while working fine on Windows, because
# npm's .cmd shims never read the shebang.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Explicit, and load-bearing: shell hooks are executed by their shebang, so
# CRLF breaks them on clone (Linux/CI). Predates the npm issue above.
.githooks/** text eol=lf
*.sh  text eol=lf
*.mjs text eol=lf
*.md  text eol=lf

# ...but Windows batch files must KEEP CRLF. Last matching rule wins, so these
# must stay below the `*` line.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf